<title>FRANCE: TF1 June audience rose slightly--French Mediamat.</title>
<headline>TF1 June audience rose slightly--French Mediamat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The audience share of TF1, France's biggest private terrestrial television channel, rose slightly in June from May while the share of public channel France 2 fell, according to a monthly survey by Mediametrie, the French audience measurement body.</p>
<p>The monthly Mediamat survey, published on Monday, also showed a rise in the tiny market share taken by other television channels, from both the previous month and June last year.</p>
<p>Mediametrie gave the following figures:</p>
<p>	   Individuals aged four and over - (in pct)</p>
<p>		     MAY 97	 JUNE 97	 JUNE 96</p>
<p>    Total TV     100	    100	     100</p>
<p>    TF1	     35.3	   35.7	    35.6</p>
<p>    France 2	23.6	   22.9	    23.9</p>
<p>    France 3	16.8	   16.8	    17.4</p>
<p>    Canal Plus     4.9	    4.6	     4.3</p>
<p>    Arte	     1.4(2.9)     1.4(2.8)	1.5(3.0)</p>
<p>    La Cinquieme   1.6(3.9)     1.8(4.1)	1.4(3.7)</p>
<p>    M6		12.7 (14.0)  13.1 (14.3)   12.4(13.5)</p>
<p>    Other TV	   3.6	    3.9	   3.5</p>
<p>			Individuals over 15 - pct</p>
<p>    Total TV	100	   100	     100</p>
<p>    TF1		34.9	  35.3	    35.5</p>
<p>    France 2	 24.6	  23.8	    24.7</p>
<p>    France 3	 16.2	  16.9	    17.4</p>
<p>    Canal Plus	5.0	   4.6	     4.3</p>
<p>    Arte		1.5(3.0)    1.5(2.9)	1.5(3.2)</p>
<p>    La Cinquieme    1.6(4.0)    1.7(4.4)	1.6(3.8)</p>
<p>    M6		 12.0(13.2)  12.4(13.3)    11.8(12.9)</p>
<p>    Other TV	  3.4	   3.6	     3.4</p>
<p>Note: The results in brackets are adjusted to take into account the fact that M6, Arte and la Cinquieme do not reach the whole population. M6 covers 91 percent, while Arte and La Cinquieme, which broadcast during the evening and the day respectively (except on some cable networks), cover 88 percent.</p>
</text>
